        <paragraph>$$f(x) = \sqrt{x + 1}$$ ; $$x = 1$$</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
    <exercise number="13" has_solution="false">
      <problem>
        <paragraph>Prove Theorem 10.</paragraph>
        <paragraph>Hint: The $$N$$ th partial sum of the Taylor series is $$S_{N}(x) = P_{N}(x)$$ , where $$P_{N}(x)$$ is the $$N$$ th Taylor polynomial. Show that $$\lim\limits_{N\rightarrow\infty}S_{N}(x) = f(x)$$ if and only if $$\lim\limits_{N\rightarrow\infty}R_{N}(x) = 0$$ .</paragraph>
      </problem>
    </exercise>
